{"name":"American Anthem","hex":"#7595ab","fetched":"2026-10-21","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"anthem","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Antiphon.","A choral or vocal composition, often with a religious or political lyric."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To celebrate with anthems."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/anthem"}],"entries":[{"title":"American Anthem","blocks":[{"text":"American Anthem is a 1986 American sports drama film directed by Albert Magnoli, starring Mitch Gaylord and Janet Jones. The film was produced by Lorimar Motion Pictures and released in North America by Columbia Pictures. Gaylord was a member of the gold medal-winning U.S. men's gymnastics team at the 1984 Summer Olympics."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/fa/American_anthem_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/American_Anthem","wikidata":"Q3083599"},{"title":"Anthem","blocks":[{"text":"An anthem is a musical composition of celebration, usually used as a symbol for a distinct group, particularly the national anthems of countries. Originally, and in music theory and religious contexts, it also refers more particularly to short sacred choral work and still more particularly to a specific form of liturgical music. In this sense, its use began c. 1550 in English-speaking churches; it uses English language words, in contrast to the originally Roman Catholic 'motet' which sets a Latin text."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anthem","wikidata":"Q541947"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/f/fa/American_anthem_poster.jpg/250px-American_anthem_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/fa/American_anthem_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/